Piece 1 — Cart module (modules/cart/)

- cart.types.ts — CartRow, CartItemRow, validators for add/update item.
- cart.service.ts — get-or-create active cart, add item, update qty, remove item, clear. Enforces single-restaurant-per-cart rule (schema: carts.restaurant_id, unique user_id). Adding an item from a different restaurant clears the cart first.
- cart.controller.ts, cart.routes.ts — customer-only (requireAuth).
- Mount /api/cart in app.ts.
- Verify: add → get → update qty → remove → cross-restaurant clear.

Piece 2 — Capacity module (modules/capacity/)

- capacity.slots.ts — currentSlotWindow(): floor now to the 15-min bucket (SLOT_MINUTES) → a Date. Redis key capacity:<restaurantId>:<slotISO>.
- capacity.service.ts — reserveSlot(restaurantId): seed the slot counter from restaurants.max_orders_per_slot on first use, atomic DECR, reject if < 0 (and INCR back on reject), set TTL so the key dies at window end. releaseSlot for rollback.
- Verify: counter decrements per reserve, blocks at 0, resets next window.
- Note: max_orders_per_slot already seeded per restaurant (seed.ts) — no reseed needed.

Piece 3 — Orders module (modules/orders/) — the race handling

- order.lock.ts — acquireLock(key): SET lock:<key> <token> NX PX <ttl>; releaseLock(key, token): Lua script that deletes only if the stored token matches (prevents releasing someone else's lock).
- utils/idempotency.ts — check/store Idempotency-Key in Redis so a retried request returns the same order instead of a duplicate.
- order.types.ts — PlaceOrderInput, validators.
- order.service.ts — placeOrder:
  a. Idempotency-Key header → if seen, return the existing order.
  b. Reserve the kitchen slot (capacity).
  c. Acquire Redis lock per menu item.
  d. Inside a DB transaction: atomic UPDATE menu_items SET stock = stock - $qty WHERE id = $1 AND stock >= $qty RETURNING * — zero rows = out of stock → 409.
  e. Create order (PENDING) + order_items snapshot; commit.
  f. Release locks (in finally); release slot if the order failed.
  g. Enqueue placeholder (Day 5 wires BullMQ; today process inline).
- order.controller.ts, order.routes.ts — customer-only. Mount /api/orders.
- Verify: place a valid order end-to-end; repeat with same Idempotency-Key → same order back.

Piece 4 — PROVE THE RACE (scripts/raceTest.ts)

- Reset a chosen menu item to stock = 1.
- Fire 20 concurrent placeOrder calls (via the service or HTTP) for that item.
- Assert exactly 1 succeeds, 19 get "out of stock".
- Print a clear result table and document the outcome.
- Verify: user runs npx tsx scripts/raceTest.ts, we confirm 1 winner / 19 losers.

